the-firm-as-one-program-lines-24 : List (List Word)
the-firm-as-one-program-lines-24 = cons "- **Q3** The quant's job is the reduction of uncertainty about unobserved (often future) events." (cons "  Predicting the vehicle count in a retail parking lot on a given day and predicting a market price are instances of the same inference problem; framing quantitative research around price series alone misstates the problem." (cons "  - **Q3.1** The problem: given environmental data, forecast subsequent environment states. The environment is the earth, the physical universe, with myriad inseparable activity within it." (cons "  - **Q3.2** Every equity, commodity and future corresponds to physical events in the real world." (cons "  - **Q3.3** Pricing is a byproduct, an observation, of complete world state. [P1]" (cons "- **Q4** The epistemic basis of prediction: no prior distribution, ever; exact inference over the present." (cons (quoted (cons "  Assuming a prior distribution is pure assumption rather than reality and cannot ground any claim of truth; a uniform prior is an even stronger ungrounded assumption than a reasoned one. Information " (cons "from tomorrow" (cons " is metaphysically nonsensical: tomorrow is undetermined now. [P1], [N2]" nil)))) (cons "  - **Q4.1** The object of analysis is not a prediction of price, since every action taken influences the world and the price." (cons "  - **Q4.2** The object is exact inference over the present: rationally exposing present information others have not." (cons "  - **Q4.3** We infer and predict the future into existence: when brains are called prediction machines, the prediction is the action; there is no separate action." (cons (quoted (cons "    predict: Latin praedicere, prae " (cons "before" (cons " + dicere " (cons "to say" (cons ", from the root *deyk- " (cons "to show, point out" (cons " (indicate, index, teach). infer: Latin inferre, " (cons "to carry into" (cons "." nil)))))))))) nil))))))))))
